  "source_profile": [
    "A new accounted native gzip Fetch adapter derived from rdgz.c; upstream rdgz.c and all zlib source remain unmodified.",
    "Two-pass unknown-length decode, first-pass output allocation before inflateEnd, second-pass initialization after first-pass cleanup, and output plus terminal NUL retained through final Fetch event.",
    "Each actual zalloc request checks product plus aligned prefix, admits before fallible malloc, and frees storage before credit release; no native allocator callback or opaque state escapes the matching stream lifetime.",
    "Inflater initialization demands admitted state before compressed input validation; the resource error therefore precedes a later checksum/format error when that initial state is denied.",
    "Source loop condition, gzip/zlib detection, terminating valid payload, ignored trailing data and first-member handling are retained. An observed full-output/no-input-or-output-progress Z_BUF_ERROR returns BAD_COMPRESSION in the accounted branch as a bounded native correction, not a claimed reference return.",
    "Resource denial, malloc failure, Z_MEM_ERROR and checked product/sum/native INT_MAX geometry return CRIT_SYS_RESOURCE; other codec errors return BAD_COMPRESSION through the existing message/error prefix and partition backoff route.",
    "Literal regression wire arrays use RFC1951 stored blocks and stdlib data-only CRC/Adler checksum construction, without running a codec, project helper, compiler or test.",
    "All regression sources remain unexecuted; LZ4/Zstd, other allocation classes, whole-native and Phase2 gates remain open."
  ],
